    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11189" root="خل" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَالٌّ</span></b>  (K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَخَلْخِلٌ</span></b>  (Mgh, K) [and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخْتَلٌّ</span></b> 
all signify <i>Having interstices, breaks, chinks,</i> or
<i>the like:</i>] <i>uncompact,</i> or <i>incoherent:</i> (Mgh, K:)
the first and second applied in this sense to an
army. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  For the first, see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَالٌ</span>, in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خيل</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُلَالَةٌ</span>.

